        "id": "ch6_3-1",
        "text": "Database Protocols\nDatabases are the center of data; black-hat hackers target mainly data during\ntheir attacks. You should consider prioritizing this process since it contains your\nclient/employer\u2019s main security risk. Application security specialists spend\nmost of their time hardening the databases. Still, what if your client/employer\nis not following this practice? Then you have plenty of fun waiting for you. This\nsection covers the following databases technologies:\nI\nI Microsoft SQL Server\nI\nI Oracle database\nI\nI MySQL\nAt this stage, you know the steps of advanced enumeration. So, for this sec-\ntion, you will learn briefly the required commands for each database vendor.\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 Microsoft SQL Server (Port 1433)\n\u2022 Oracle Database Server (Port 1521)\n\u2022 MySQL (Port 3306)\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
